    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d665">

                <pb facs="0568" n="452" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg452"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/11487.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Chargé O’Shaughnessy.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-11T21:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 11, 1914, 9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>741. Your No. 842, April 11, 1 p.m. I communicated Admiral Mayo’s ultimatum to
                    the President and he approved demand made. My telegram 740 of April 10, 9 p.m.,
                    to you was in part expressed in the language of the President.</p>
                <p>The statement by Huerta as quoted in your No. 841, April 10, 8 p.m., does not
                    meet the last part of the demand and I notified Mr. Algara, the Mexican Chargé
                    here, of this fact about noon to-day.</p>
                <p>This Government appreciates, however, the difficulty of securing prompt action
                    during the religious exercises connected with Holy Week and if General Huerta
                    gives this as a reason for not having complied, this Government will direct
                    Admiral Mayo to extend the time until Monday evening.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
